     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like it may be a mistake.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day** of metformin. The maximum labeled dose is **2550 mg/day** for immediate-release and **2000 mg/day** for extended-release, so this is twice the maximum. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI side effects, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**What you might have meant:**\n1. **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the IR maximum). If 1700 mg was meant as the daily total, this matches that intent.\n2. **850 mg by mouth twice daily with meals** (1700 mg/day total), a common maintenance dose.\n3. **1700 mg/day split some other way**, or an extended-release form. Let me know the dose, frequency and formulation.\n\nPlease confirm which one you want, or send the correct dose and frequency, and I'll enter it. If you really do mean 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed the dose above the maximum. I'd recommend a pharmacy review first, though."
      }
     ],
